{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/api/books?bibkeys=OLID:OL9245413M,ISBN:006251587X&jscmd=details&format=json","file":"data/metadata1000_261025/raw/library-416cd8f4fa8d5d39.json","retrieved":"2026-10-25T14:29:00.617Z","status":200,"data":{"OLID:OL9245413M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL9245413M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9245413M/Weaving_the_Web","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9245413M/Weaving_the_Web","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/48834-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Collins"],"number_of_pages":256,"subtitle":"The Original Design and Ultimate Destiny of the World Wide Web","weight":"6.9 ounces","covers":[48834],"physical_format":"Paperback","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-11-10T07:59:10.547299"},"latest_revision":8,"key":"/books/OL9245413M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL25245A","name":"Tim Berners-Lee"}],"subjects":["Internet - World Wide Web","General","Computer Books: Web Programming","Computers","Computer - Internet","World Wide Web","History","E-Commerce - General","Business & Economics / General","Computer Bks - Internet","Berners-Lee, Tim"],"edition_name":"1 edition","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"When I first began tinkering with a software program that even gave rise to the idea of the World Wide Web, I named it Enquire, short for Enquire Within upon Everything, a musty old book of Victorian advice I noticed as a child in my parents' house outside\""},"source_records":["amazon:006251587X:o-4:281104653:250026","amazon:006251587X:4:3728623887:262825"],"title":"Weaving the Web","identifiers":{"librarything":["2059"],"goodreads":["821987"]},"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"isbn_13":["9780062515872"],"isbn_10":["006251587X"],"publish_date":"November 7, 2000","works":[{"key":"/works/OL158398W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8 x 5.3 x 0.6 inches","revision":8}},"ISBN:006251587X":{"bib_key":"ISBN:006251587X","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL38986M/Weaving_the_Web","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780062515872","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9695142-S.jpg","details":{"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Tim Berners-Lee, the inventor of the World Wide Web, has been hailed by Time magazine as one of the 100 greatest minds of this century. His creation has already changed the way people do business, entertain themselves, exchange ideas, and socialize with one another.\"--BOOK JACKET.\n\n\"Berners-Lee offers insights to help readers understand the true nature of the Web, enabling them to use it to their fullest advantage. He shares his views on such critical issues as censorship, privacy, the increasing power of software companies in the online world, and the need to find the ideal balance between the commercial and social forces on the Web. His criticism of the Web's current state makes clear that there is still much work to be done.\n\nFinally, Berners-Lee presents his own plan for the Web's future, one that calls for the active support and participation of programmers, computer manufacturers, and social organizations to make it happen.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes index."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["2059"],"wikidata":["Q3988193","Q126546787"],"goodreads":["1308515","821987"]},"title":"Weaving the Web","subtitle":"the original design and ultimate destiny of the World Wide Web by its inventor","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL25245A","name":"Tim Berners-Lee"}],"publish_date":"1999","publishers":["HarperSanFrancisco"],"ia_box_id":["IA105701"],"covers":[9695142],"url":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/description/hc044/99027665.html"],"publish_places":["San Francisco, USA"],"contributions":["Fischetti, Mark."],"subjects":["Berners-Lee, Tim","World Wide Web -- History"],"uri_descriptions":["Publisher description"],"la